cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this CIT-K kernel or the Cat Intelligence (HIM) theory in your research, please cite the works below."
title: "CIT-K: Cognitive Internal Theory — Kernel (Minimal Zero-Network Kernel)"
abstract: >-
  CIT-K is a ~119-line, zero-network, zero-gradient, zero-content-pretraining
  autonomous-motivation agent driven solely by a single computable comfort
  gradient. It starts from a blank newborn, learns only by passive causal
  memory, and self-emerges a world model and an exploration-homecoming
  alternation without external reward, preset goal, or neural network.
